  {
   "evidence": "The conclusion is `\u2016((-1) ^ n / n ! : \u2102) \u2022 iteratedDeriv n F z\u2016 + (((-1) ^ n / n ! : \u2102) \u2022 iteratedDeriv n F z.re).re \u2264 ...`. By `integrableOn_and_re_laplace_coeff_eq`, the second summand equals `\u222b g u * w u`, which is negative whenever `g` is negative, so the first summand alone can exceed the right-hand side.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/LaplaceTransform/WindowCoefficients.lean",
   "fix": "Reword it to match the statement, e.g. \"Bound the norm of the signed Laplace coefficient at `z` plus the real part of the coefficient at `z.re` by twice the damped positive part on the window `(U, V]` plus a Gamma-weighted tail.\"",
   "issue": "The docstring opens with \"Bound a signed Laplace coefficient by the integral of the damped positive part on a window and a Gamma-weighted tail\". The statement actually bounds `\u2016a_n(z)\u2016 + Re a_n(z.re)`. The second term can be negative, so the theorem does not bound the coefficient by itself, and a reader taking the docstring at face value would misuse the result.",
   "line": 92
  }
 ],
